<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">People's Republic of China</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The People's Republic of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a> is the state founded by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chinese-communist-party">Chinese Communist Party</a> in 1949. Its territory largely corresponds to that defined by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qing-empire">Qing Empire</a>, which incorporated <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/xinjiang">Xinjiang</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tibet">Tibet</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mongolia">Mongolia</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manchuria">Manchuria</a> into the Chinese imperial state. The site's Qing Empire profile describes this territorial framework as the dynasty's most enduring geopolitical legacy.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/peoples-republic-of-china.jpg" alt="People's Republic of China" width="320" height="214" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Zeng Liansong · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_the_People%27s_Republic_of_China.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
